 "title": "Metal Clang",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: a struck, metallic, out-of-tune hit, the clanging 'sampled scrap metal' of industrial music, made with no samples at all.\n\nHow it's built: a Ring Mod multiplies two oscillators tuned an odd interval apart, which gives inharmonic tones like struck metal; a band-pass filter picks a band of them; a short envelope strikes it; Drive and a big Reverb make it hang in a warehouse.\n\nPlay: single notes and clusters, low and high.\n\nTweak: the second oscillator's TUNE (every setting is a different piece of metal), the filter's CUTOFF, the reverb's SIZE.",
